@startuml feature_v1.2.0_F-009_sequence
' Runtime truth for F-009 v1.2.0 — Client Surfaces occ CLI and MCP
' Reconstructed from shipped code. Arrows name contracts the hub documents;
' a value not configured anywhere in the repository is written OPEN, never guessed.
' The cast below is the participants: list of feature_v1.2.0_F-009_front-matter.yaml, name for name.
title F-009 v1.2.0 — Client Surfaces occ CLI and MCP
autonumber

actor "Developer" as Dev
actor "AI agent" as Agent
participant "occ CLI" as OCC
participant "generated OpenAPI client" as Gen
participant "MCP server" as MCP
participant "MCP handlers" as MH
participant "openchoreo-api" as API
participant "service layer" as Svc
participant "audit middleware" as Audit
database "Kubernetes API (etcd)" as K8s

group F-009-US1 — one CLI for every platform resource, with the same shape as the API
  Dev -> OCC : occ login
  activate OCC
  OCC -> API : OIDC authorization code with PKCE
  API --> OCC : token
  deactivate OCC
  Dev -> OCC : occ <kind> <verb>
  activate OCC
  OCC -> Gen : typed call
  Gen -> API : HTTP request against the generated contract
  API -> Audit : record the operation
  API -> Svc : dispatch
  Svc -> K8s : read or write the custom resource
  K8s --> Svc : result
  Svc --> API : result
  API --> Gen : response
  Gen --> OCC : typed result
  OCC --> Dev : rendered output
  deactivate OCC
end

group F-009-US2 — operate the platform through typed tools rather than by shelling out
  Agent -> MCP : call a registered tool
  activate MCP
  MCP -> MCP : authenticate the bearer token
  MCP -> MH : dispatch to the toolset handler
  MH -> Svc : the same service the HTTP handler calls
  Svc -> K8s : read or write
  K8s --> Svc : result
  Svc --> MH : result
  MH --> MCP : JSON-encoded result
  MCP --> Agent : tool result
  deactivate MCP
  alt unauthenticated
    MCP --> Agent : unauthenticated, with the protected-resource metadata URL
  end
end

group F-009-US3 — every action is audited identically whoever performed it
  Audit -> Audit : resolve the operation from the generated definitions table
  alt the operation is exempt
    Audit -> Audit : no event emitted
  else
    Audit -> Audit : emit an audit event with surface and user agent
  end
  note right of Audit : MCP calls resolve through their own bindings beside the HTTP definitions
end

group failure — the control plane is unreachable
  Gen -> API : request
  API --> Gen : transport error
  Gen --> OCC : error surfaced to the user, no partial local state is written
end

note over MCP, Svc
  invariants: DOM-002-R4 the request context is serialised once per request
  DOM-002-R5 exec and wirelogs authenticate outside the standard middleware order
  the CLI and MCP are two presentations of one service layer, audited through one generated table
  OPEN: no client timeout or retry policy is configured
  OPEN: the selection rule behind 25 MCP tools over 214 API operations is unstated
  OPEN: which tools are safe for an unattended agent is unstated
end note
@enduml
